[DESCRIPTION]
.B andersen-mqtt
connects to an Andersen window controller through a TCP serial gateway, polls
the status of its four windows, and publishes each window's state to an MQTT
broker. Commands published to a window's command topic open, close or stop
that window.
.PP
On a server it runs as a systemd service, described under
.BR SERVICE .
The options below are for running it by hand.

[SERVICE]
The package installs and enables
.BR andersen-mqtt.service ,
which runs
.B andersen-mqtt
with the configuration file listed under
.B FILES
as a dynamically allocated user. It is started when the package is installed
and restarted when the package is upgraded.
.PP
The program does not reconnect by itself. It exits with a failure status when
it loses the MQTT broker (including when another client connects with the same
.BR mqtt.clientId ),
when the broker refuses the connection or hasn't completed it within 30
seconds, when the gateway closes the connection,
or when no status arrives from the window controller for three poll intervals
(at least 30 seconds). systemd then starts it again after ten seconds. It exits
cleanly on
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT .

[CONFIGURATION]
The configuration file is a JSON object. Every key is optional, and a missing
key keeps the default shown below. An unknown key, or a value of the wrong
type, stops the program at startup rather than being ignored.
.TP
.B mqtt.host
MQTT broker host name or address. Default
.BR 10.3.2.5 .
.TP
.B mqtt.port
MQTT broker port. Default
.BR 1883 .
.TP
.B mqtt.clientId
MQTT client identifier. Default
.BR andersen\-mqtt .
Two clients with the same identifier disconnect each other, so give each
running copy its own.
.TP
.B mqtt.topicPrefix
Prefix for every topic. Default
.BR andersen\-mqtt/windows .
.TP
.B gateway.host
Host name or address of the TCP serial gateway attached to the window
controller. Default
.BR 10.3.2.5 .
.TP
.B gateway.port
Gateway TCP port. Default
.BR 6000 .
.TP
.B pollIntervalSeconds
Seconds between status polls, from 1 to 3600. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.B logLevel
One of
.BR trace ,
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warning ,
.BR error ,
.BR critical ,
or
.BR off .
Default
.BR info .
The
.B \-\-log\-level
option overrides it.

[TOPICS]
Each window is named
.B window1
to
.BR window4 .
For a window
.IR NAME ,
the program publishes retained messages to
.IR PREFIX / NAME /open ,
.BR movement_obstructed ,
.BR screen_missing ,
.BR rf_heard ,
.BR rain_sensed
and
.B rain_override_active
(each
.B yes
or
.BR no ),
and
.B last_polled
(an ISO 8601 time). It publishes when a value changes, and every value once
after starting.
.PP
It subscribes to
.IR PREFIX / NAME /command .
A message starting with
.B o
opens the window,
.B c
closes it, and
.B s
stops it, in either case, so Home Assistant's default
.BR OPEN ,
.B CLOSE
and
.B STOP
payloads work. Retained messages on a command topic are ignored, since the
broker would replay them every time the program starts; publish commands
without the retain flag.

[FILES]
.TP
.I /etc/andersen\-mqtt/andersen\-mqtt.json
Configuration file, read by the service. Upgrades keep local changes.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/andersen\-mqtt.service
The systemd unit. Override it with a drop\-in under
.IR /etc/systemd/system/andersen\-mqtt.service.d/ .

[EXAMPLES]
Run in the foreground against a test configuration, with debug logging:
.PP
.RS
.nf
andersen\-mqtt \-\-config ./test.json \-\-log\-level debug
.fi
.RE
.PP
Watch the service, and every topic it publishes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
journalctl \-u andersen\-mqtt.service \-f
mosquitto_sub \-h 10.3.2.5 \-t 'andersen\-mqtt/windows/#' \-v
.fi
.RE
.PP
Open the first window:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mosquitto_pub \-h 10.3.2.5 \-t andersen\-mqtt/windows/window1/command \-m open
.fi
.RE

[SEE ALSO]
.BR systemd.unit (5)
